\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Change query interaction in HCE. Paired states, directed difference, and absolute difference are projected into dense feature \(Z_i\), flattened into \(T_i\), and processed by query and spatial-token updates. A residual FFN and dense residual then produce change output \(D_i\). \(Q_i^0/Q_i^1\) denote queries before/after updating; \(C\) and plus signs denote concatenation and addition. Local connections in the working figure await correction; the text defines the computation.}}{14}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cqi}{{4}{14}{Change query interaction in HCE. Paired states, directed difference, and absolute difference are projected into dense feature \(Z_i\), flattened into \(T_i\), and processed by query and spatial-token updates. A residual FFN and dense residual then produce change output \(D_i\). \(Q_i^0/Q_i^1\) denote queries before/after updating; \(C\) and plus signs denote concatenation and addition. Local connections in the working figure await correction; the text defines the computation}{figure.caption.5}{}}
